From 11a591018c5907304796cbe42899ed9c679b1e7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sh1neSp4rk <Sh1neSp4rk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:20:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Steam Frame: fix Halo 3 stereo, weapon flicker and in-game
 tuning

Halo 3 eye cover (the "cross-eyed / zoomed" fix): render both eyes with one
symmetric cover, 1% wider than the widest native edge of either eye. The
per-eye cover was published as one value (the last eye rendered), so the left
eye failed containment and both slices went out at the right eye's cover FOV,
which the Frame's compositor shows warped. Halo 3 now takes the native
per-eye FOV + sub-rect path, as ODST already did.

FP weapon flicker (right eye): keep each slot's interpolation context until a
successful interpolation replaces it, and pose palette submissions with no
matching context from the last pose of the same render model (arms and weapon
are separate tags). FRAME_FP_REUSE=0 restores the stock behaviour.

Tuning without a keyboard: FRAME_WORLD_SCALE sets the starting Halo 3 world
scale, FRAME_STEREO_SCALE multiplies eye separation only.

Diagnostics: FRAME-FLICKER counters and a one-shot draw-order trace, L3/R3
edge logging, and dump_eyes.flag (writes both eye caches as BMPs).
Menu: hide the duplicate "Quality of Life" page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
